    {
      "html": "<ul class=\"flex flex-col gap-6\"><li class=\"flex flex-col gap-2\"><h3 class=\"text-xl text-gray-300\"><a class=\"active:brightness-75 underline\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://www.cmrg.me\">cmrg.me</a></h3><p>you are looking at it. after years of rewriting this website, the talk has finally given me a deadline i cannot move. much of its argument comes from what i built and learned here, so this version needs to be finished and released before i can call the slides done</p></li><li class=\"flex flex-col gap-2\"><h3 class=\"text-xl text-gray-300\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"font-mono tracking-tighter text-gray-500 blur-sm brightness-150 contrast-150\">redacted</span><span class=\"sr-only\">an upcoming talk</span></h3><p>an upcoming talk for a conference here in Brazil. every change to the site either gives me another example or ruins a slide i thought was done, and every new idea for the slides gives Metope something else to support. the title stays hidden until i can change the site without reopening the slides</p></li><li class=\"flex flex-col gap-2\"><h3 class=\"text-xl text-gray-300\">Metope</h3><p>the talk only works if Metope does. it remains private for a few more weeks. once the talk and site are done, i need a little time to recover from both and finish the structure i have in mind before releasing it. until then, its first serious test is powering that talk at a conference with more than 2,000 people. almost no pressure at all</p></li></ul>",
